From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Map the macOS Main words through both
 firmware layouts

macOS 26B123 on this machine runs its own build of the GPU firmware,
and its Main object does not use the same offsets as the 25G83 build
we load. The g16_main_macos table read macOS's words with one constant
shift, which the two builds' INIT copy routines show to be wrong in
places: the field that 25G83 reads at +0xe90..+0xeb4 sits 0x120 bytes
higher in 26B123, the fields from +0xec0 0x11c higher, and +0x2604 /
+0x2608 0x120 higher again. Five of the old entries were loader records,
which only a by-name slot map can place.

Rebuild the table from a per-field map. Every entry pairs one of our
offsets with macOS's value at the matching 26B123 offset, proven by the
two INIT routines or bracketed by proven fields with the same shift and
agreeing values. The table now starts with the seven entries the INIT
routines prove. Words in stretches where the shift is not proven are
left out, as are the loader records. The table goes from 131 words to
105. The switch stays off by default.

Assisted-by: LLM
